<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simon Vratsian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1969</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simon Vratsian was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenian-revolutionary-federation">Armenian Revolutionary Federation</a> politician and the last prime minister of the First Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, taking office in November 1920 as Turkish and Red armies closed in. After the Soviet takeover he joined the rising of 1921 and the Republic of Mountainous Armenia led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garegin-nzhdeh">Garegin Nzhdeh</a>, then spent the rest of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-vratsian.jpg" alt="Simon Vratsian" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simon_Vratsian.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
